+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+Defines how an RFC 6902 JSON Patch is validated and applied to a JSON document, producing a new document without modifying the inputs.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Patch document structure
+Per RFC 6902 §3, a patch SHALL be an array of operation objects. Each operation SHALL have a string `op` that is one of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test` and a string `path` that is a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Members not defined for the operation SHALL be ignored. Operations are applied in order. Any violation SHALL cause an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Empty patch
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[]`
+- **THEN** the result equals the document
+
+#### Scenario: Patch is not an array
+- **WHEN** the patch is an object, `null`, a string or `undefined`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Operation is not an object
+- **WHEN** an element is `null`, an array or a scalar
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown or missing op
+- **WHEN** `op` is missing, not a string, or not one of the six names (e.g. `"merge"`, `"ADD"`)
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or invalid path
+- **WHEN** `path` is missing, not a string, or not a valid JSON Pointer (e.g. `"a"`, `"/a~2"`)
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing value
+- **WHEN** an `add`, `replace` or `test` operation has no `value` member (RFC 6902 §4.1, §4.3, §4.6)
+- **THEN** an error is thrown, whereas `"value": null` is a valid value
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or invalid from
+- **WHEN** a `move` or `copy` operation has no `from` member, or it is not a valid JSON Pointer (§4.4, §4.5)
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Unrecognised members
+- **WHEN** an operation carries extra members such as `"comment"`
+- **THEN** they are ignored
+
+### Requirement: Inputs are not mutated
+`applyPatch` SHALL return a new value and SHALL NOT modify the document or the patch. The result SHALL NOT share mutable structure with the document or with the patch's `value`s, so that changing the result later cannot alter either input.
+
+#### Scenario: Document unchanged
+- **WHEN** a patch with any operations is applied to a document
+- **THEN** the document is deep-equal to a copy taken beforehand
+
+#### Scenario: Values are copied
+- **WHEN** an `add` inserts an object `value`, and the result is then modified
+- **THEN** the patch's `value` is unchanged
+
+### Requirement: Atomic application
+Per RFC 6902 §5, if any operation fails, an error SHALL be thrown and no result returned; operations before the failure have no observable effect.
+
+#### Scenario: Later operation fails
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":1},{"op":"remove","path":"/missing"}]`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and the document is unchanged
+
+### Requirement: add
+Per RFC 6902 §4.1, `add` SHALL insert `value` at `path`. The parent of the target SHALL exist. For an object parent the member is added, or replaced if it already exists. For an array parent the value is inserted before the given index, shifting later elements; the index SHALL be a valid array index (RFC 6901 §4: no leading zeros, no sign) not greater than the array length; the token `-` appends. If `path` is `""` the whole document is replaced by `value`.
+
+#### Scenario: Add object member
+- **WHEN** adding `/baz` = `"qux"` to `{"foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":"bar","baz":"qux"}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add replaces existing member
+- **WHEN** adding `/foo` = `1` to `{"foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":1}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add into array
+- **WHEN** adding `/foo/1` = `"qux"` to `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["bar","qux","baz"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add at array end
+- **WHEN** adding `/foo/-` = `"x"`, and separately `/foo/2`, to `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** both give `{"foo":["bar","baz","x"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add index out of range or malformed
+- **WHEN** the index is greater than the length (`/foo/3`), negative, `01`, `1.0`, or not numeric
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Add with missing parent
+- **WHEN** adding `/baz/bat` to `{"foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Add replaces whole document
+- **WHEN** the path is `""` and value is `[1]`
+- **THEN** the result is `[1]`
+
+#### Scenario: Add below a scalar
+- **WHEN** the parent of the target is a string, number, boolean or `null`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: remove
+Per RFC 6902 §4.2, `remove` SHALL delete the value at `path`, which MUST exist. Removing an array element shifts later elements down. Removing the whole document (`path` `""`) leaves no JSON value to return and SHALL be an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Remove object member
+- **WHEN** removing `/baz` from `{"baz":"qux","foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":"bar"}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove array element
+- **WHEN** removing `/foo/1` from `{"foo":["bar","qux","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove nonexistent target
+- **WHEN** the member does not exist, the index is out of range, or the index is `-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Remove root
+- **WHEN** the path is `""`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace
+Per RFC 6902 §4.3, `replace` SHALL set the value at `path`, which MUST exist, to `value`. Path `""` replaces the whole document.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace member
+- **WHEN** replacing `/baz` with `"boo"` in `{"baz":"qux","foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"baz":"boo","foo":"bar"}`
+
+#### Scenario: Replace array element
+- **WHEN** replacing `/foo/0` with `"x"` in `{"foo":["a","b"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["x","b"]}` with the array length unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Replace nonexistent target
+- **WHEN** the member does not exist, or the array index is out of range or `-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Replace root
+- **WHEN** the path is `""`
+- **THEN** the result is `value`
+
+### Requirement: move
+Per RFC 6902 §4.4, `move` SHALL remove the value at `from` (which MUST exist) and add it at `path`, as `remove` followed by `add`. `from` SHALL NOT be a proper prefix of `path`. Moving a location onto itself leaves the document unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Move object member
+- **WHEN** moving `/foo/waldo` to `/qux/thud` in `{"foo":{"bar":"baz","waldo":"fred"},"qux":{"corge":"grault"}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":{"bar":"baz"},"qux":{"corge":"grault","thud":"fred"}}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move array element
+- **WHEN** moving `/foo/1` to `/foo/3` in `{"foo":["all","grass","cows","eat"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["all","cows","eat","grass"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move from nonexistent location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `from` is `/a` and `path` is `/a/b`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move onto itself
+- **WHEN** `from` equals `path` and exists
+- **THEN** the result equals the document
+
+### Requirement: copy
+Per RFC 6902 §4.5, `copy` SHALL add a deep copy of the value at `from` (which MUST exist) at `path`, as in `add`.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy member
+- **WHEN** copying `/foo` to `/bar` in `{"foo":{"a":1}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":{"a":1},"bar":{"a":1}}`
+
+#### Scenario: Copy is independent
+- **WHEN** a copied object is then changed by a later operation in the same patch
+- **THEN** the original location is unaffected
+
+#### Scenario: Copy from nonexistent location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: test
+Per RFC 6902 §4.6 and §5, `test` SHALL succeed, leaving the document unchanged, only if the value at `path` (which MUST exist) equals `value`; otherwise an error is thrown. Equality: same type; strings equal code-point for code-point; numbers equal by numeric value; booleans and `null` identical; arrays equal if same length and elements equal in order; objects equal if same set of member names and equal values, regardless of member order.
+
+#### Scenario: Matching values
+- **WHEN** testing `/a` against `{"a":{"x":[1,2],"y":null}}` with value `{"y":null,"x":[1,2]}`
+- **THEN** the patch applies successfully
+
+#### Scenario: Type mismatch
+- **WHEN** testing a number `1` against `"1"`, `null` against `0`, or `[]` against `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Array order matters
+- **WHEN** `[1,2]` is tested against `[2,1]`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing target
+- **WHEN** the path does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Test root
+- **WHEN** path is `""` and value equals the document
+- **THEN** the patch applies successfully
+
+### Requirement: Pointer escaping and hostile keys
+Paths and `from` SHALL be evaluated with RFC 6901 escaping (`~0`, `~1`). Keys such as `__proto__`, `constructor` and `toString` SHALL be treated as ordinary member names: they never reach or alter prototypes, and only own members count as existing.
+
+#### Scenario: Escaped keys
+- **WHEN** adding `/a~1b` and `/m~0n` to `{}`
+- **THEN** the result has own members `"a/b"` and `"m~n"`
+
+#### Scenario: __proto__ member
+- **WHEN** adding `/__proto__/polluted` = `true` to `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown (no such member) and `Object.prototype` is unmodified
+
+#### Scenario: __proto__ as a key
+- **WHEN** adding `/__proto__` = `{"x":1}` to `{}`
+- **THEN** the result has an own member `"__proto__"` and `({}).x` is `undefined`
+
+#### Scenario: Inherited names do not exist
+- **WHEN** removing, replacing or testing `/toString` or `/constructor` on `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Error type
+All failures SHALL throw an `Error` subclass `JsonPatchError`, exported from the package entry point.
+
+#### Scenario: Failure type
+- **WHEN** a patch is invalid or an operation fails
+- **THEN** the thrown error is an instance of `JsonPatchError`
